    "created_at": "2026-11-28T00:27:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-28T00:27:43Z",
    "body": "One more requirement for the mirror:\n\n**Thread hand.** Under `GeometricMirror`, the reflected helix of a thread mill or a helical bore changes hand: a right-hand thread becomes a left-hand thread. The scope refuses \"threading\". Please name these cases in the refusal list too, so that a mirrored copy can never cut a thread of the wrong hand:\n- thread milling operations;\n- tapping cycles (G84, G74 and the dialect forms);\n- any helical move whose hand is part of the result.\n\nUnder `PreserveClimb`, a reversed helix also changes the thread hand, so the same refusal applies there.\n\nDone means adds: a test that a thread-milling operation in a mirror folder is refused by name in both cut-direction modes.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
